.SS " bool jinja2\&.sandbox\&.SandboxedEnvironment\&.is_safe_attribute ( self, t\&.Any obj, str attr, t\&.Any value)"

.PP
.nf
The sandboxed environment will call this method to check if the
attribute of an object is safe to access\&.  Per default all attributes
starting with an underscore are considered private as well as the
special attributes of internal python objects as returned by the
:func:`is_internal_attribute` function\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBjinja2\&.sandbox\&.ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment\fP\&.
.SS " bool jinja2\&.sandbox\&.SandboxedEnvironment\&.is_safe_callable ( self, t\&.Any obj)"

.PP
.nf
Check if an object is safely callable\&. By default callables
are considered safe unless decorated with :func:`unsafe`\&.

This also recognizes the Django convention of setting
``func\&.alters_data = True``\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBUndefined\fP jinja2\&.sandbox\&.SandboxedEnvironment\&.unsafe_undefined ( self, t\&.Any obj, str attribute)"

.PP
.nf
Return an undefined object for unsafe attributes\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SS " t\&.Optional[t\&.Callable[\&.\&.\&., str]] jinja2\&.sandbox\&.SandboxedEnvironment\&.wrap_str_format ( self, t\&.Any value)"

.PP
.nf
If the given value is a ``str\&.format`` or ``str\&.format_map`` method,
return a new function than handles sandboxing\&. This is done at access
rather than in :meth:`call`, so that calls made without ``call`` are
also sandboxed\&.

.fi
